name: sim.createIkGroup
description: Creates an IK group.
luaSynopsis: int ikGroupHandle=sim.createIkGroup(int options,int[] intParams=nil,float[] floatParams=nil)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. options: bit-coded options:
2. bit 0 set (1): the group is inactive.
3. bit 1 set (2): joint limits are taken into account during calculation (i.e. only for redundant kinematics).
4. bit 2 set (4): restore if position not reached.
5. bit 3 set (8): restore if orientation not reached.
6. bit 4 set (16): do not ignore the joint's max. step sizes.
7. bit 5 set (32): the group is explicitly handled.
8. intParams: an optional array of 2 integer parameters (i.e. array can be nullptr):
9. intParams[0]: the IK calculation method.
10. intParams[1]: the maximum number of iterations.
11. floatParams: an optional array of 4 double parameters (i.e. array can be nullptr):
12. floatParams[0]: the damping factor.
13. floatParams[1]: the joint limit weight.
14. floatParams[2]: the prismatic joint limit threshold.
15. floatParams[3]: the revolute joint limit threshold.
16. reserved: reserved. Set to nullptr.
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. -1 if operation was not successful, otherwise the IK group handle.
